NOTE: Everything works perfect in locally but in production the email sending
features doesn't work, most probably due to the use of frii.site domain that I used
for Mailtrap. 
The use of the free frii.site domain is the most probable reason your emails are not being delivered to real inboxes.

While my configuration with Mailtrap is correct and your DNS records are likely set up properly for sending, the domain name itself seems to be 
the issue. Major email providers like Gmail, Yahoo, and Outlook treat emails coming from free, lesser-known domains with extreme suspicion, often 
blocking them or marking them as spam before they ever reach a user's inbox.

Since I couldn't find any fault with the inputs and code, this is the only problem I could identify with this project's code.

Solution: Use a credible and relevant domain to send mailtrap emails.